                "entry_id": "1f5d7272-1363-3c8b-b8a7-cbcd671d41bc",
                "word": "paleographer",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c49c584b-e83d-4f5f-9f14-6fae5b3974ab",
                        "entry_id": "1f5d7272-1363-3c8b-b8a7-cbcd671d41bc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "paleographers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c2e1c016-d92c-35a8-b71b-d59f9973d895",
                        "entry_id": "1f5d7272-1363-3c8b-b8a7-cbcd671d41bc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person skilled in paleography."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "08f0a7f7-beef-4d49-87a6-207248ba70e1",
                                "sense_id": "c2e1c016-d92c-35a8-b71b-d59f9973d895",
                                "text": "Paleography might teach men to read documents, diplomatics to date them and to test their authenticity; but the full significance of an ancient deed might easily escape the most exact paleographer and the most accomplished diplomatist, for the want of that finished sense for legal technicality which is the natural fruit of a conveyancing practice."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "45c13fa2-f73b-4f9a-887d-0daf894c12c9",
                                "sense_id": "c2e1c016-d92c-35a8-b71b-d59f9973d895",
                                "text": "Finally Mark reports Christ as saying, after his resurrection, that those who believe in him will be saved and those who do not, damned; but it is impossible to discover whether he means anything by a state of damnation beyond a state of error. The paleographers regard this passage as tacked on by a later scribe. On the whole Mark leaves the modern reader where Matthew left him."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cf9e46a0-ab39-4dde-b0fe-289f29bfdf51",
                        "source_entry_id": "1f5d7272-1363-3c8b-b8a7-cbcd671d41bc",
                        "source_sense_id": "c2e1c016-d92c-35a8-b71b-d59f9973d895",
                        "source_sense_description": "a person skilled in paleography",
                        "target_lang_word": "paléographe",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "paléographe",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "87344a51-fbd6-37b5-a83f-b699c54de838",
                                        "entry_id": "775247f0-2378-3e3c-b9fd-4294a88be21b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Celui, celle qui est versé dans la paléographie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1b771b0-f142-4399-8504-09d00f724311",
                                                "sense_id": "87344a51-fbd6-37b5-a83f-b699c54de838",
                                                "text": "Avec la patience et l’acharnement d’un paléographe, le juge valognais en avait pesé chaque terme, soucieux d’y trouver quelque anachronisme, indice probable de la non-authenticité du document, en tout cas de sa post-fabrication."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2aec5f1-843c-48ed-ad75-bfba400a3bae",
                                                "sense_id": "87344a51-fbd6-37b5-a83f-b699c54de838",
                                                "text": "Les archives européennes débordent littéralement de documents juridiques encore à découvrir, conservés dans des boîtes poussiéreuses. Ce qui manque, c’est une nouvelle génération d’historiens capables de les analyser et de paléographes capables de lire les écritures manuscrites."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "27abdd3e-dd41-30bc-b52b-338e00dfbea3",
                                        "entry_id": "775247f0-2378-3e3c-b9fd-4294a88be21b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Par apposition,"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ec7c13c-6713-45c8-9a2e-7536b9cbbb40",
                                                "sense_id": "27abdd3e-dd41-30bc-b52b-338e00dfbea3",
                                                "text": "Archiviste paléographe, Ancien élève diplômé de l’École des chartes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10751493-d7cc-4c10-a9a9-524923b12f9c",
                                                "sense_id": "27abdd3e-dd41-30bc-b52b-338e00dfbea3",
                                                "text": "Je dus constater que la chaleur agit sur les ailes d’une mouche tout autrement que sur le cerveau d’un archiviste paléographe, car j’éprouvais une grande difficulté à penser et une torpeur assez agréable dont je ne sortis que par un effort violent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
